Here is the SQL query in LaTeX format:
\begin{verbatim}
SELECT meeting_name, meeting_location, meeting_date, COUNT(DISTINCT attendees) AS number_of_attendees, AVG(duration_minutes) AS average_duration
FROM meeting
WHERE meeting_date BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
GROUP BY meeting_name, meeting_location, meeting_date
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN attendees IN (SELECT DISTINCT department FROM employee) THEN department END) > 1;
\end{verbatim}
This query will return the meeting names, locations, and dates for meetings where attendees were from different departments, and the meeting date was between January 1st, 2020 and December 31st, 2020. Additionally, the query includes a table that shows the number of attendees for each meeting and the average duration of the meeting.
