What is the best way to sort a list of objects in C# based on a specific property? Here is a sample list of objects:
List<Car> cars = new List<Car>();
cars.Add(new Car("Ford", "Mustang", 2019));
cars.Add(new Car("Chevrolet", "Corvette", 2021));
cars.Add(new Car("Dodge", "Challenger", 2020));
I want to sort this list based on the "Year" property of the Car object. How can I achieve this using C# code?

output:
You can use the LINQ library in C# to sort the list of Car objects based on the "Year" property. Here is an example code snippet that demonstrates how to do this:
```
using System.Linq;
// Define the Car class
public class Car
{
    public string Make { get; set; }
    public string Model { get; set; }
    public int Year { get; set; }
    public Car(string make, string model, int year)
    {
        Make = make;
        Model = model;
        Year = year;
    }
}
// Create a list of Car objects
List<Car> cars = new List<Car>();
cars.Add(new Car("Ford", "Mustang", 2019));
cars.Add(new Car("Chevrolet", "Corvette", 2021));
cars.Add(new Car("Dodge", "Challenger", 2020));
// Sort the list based on the Year property
var sortedCars = cars.OrderBy(car => car.Year);
// Iterate over the sorted list and print the results
foreach (var car in sortedCars)
{
    Console.WriteLine($"{car.Year} {car.Make} {car.Model}");
}
```
In this code snippet, we use the `OrderBy` method from the LINQ library to sort the list of Car objects based on the "Year" property. The lambda expression `car => car.Year` specifies the property to sort by. The `sortedCars` variable contains the sorted list of Car objects. Finally, we iterate over the sorted list using a `foreach` loop and print the results to the console.

