To transform a given sentence into active voice using Markdown, you can use the following steps:
1. Identify the subject, verb, and object of the sentence.
2. Rewrite the sentence in active voice by putting the subject before the verb and the object after the verb.
3. Use Markdown to format the output as needed.
Here's an example Java code snippet that demonstrates this:
```java
String sentence = "[Passive voice] The car was driven by the woman.";
String[] words = sentence.split(" ");
String subject = "";
String verb = "";
String object = "";
String output = "";
for (int i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {
    String word = words[i];
    if (word.equals("by")) {
        // The subject is the word before "by"
        subject = words[i-1];
        // The verb is the word after "was"
        verb = words[i+1];
        // The object is the words after the verb
        for (int j = i+2; j < words.length; j++) {
            object += words[j] + " ";
        }
        // Remove the extra space at the end of the object
        object = object.trim();
        break;
    }
}
output = subject + " " + verb + " " + object;
output = output.replace("[Passive voice]", "");
output = "**" + output + "**";
System.out.println(output);
```
This code will output "**The woman drove the car.**" in active voice and in bold using Markdown.

