How can we use Go to implement a spam email detection algorithm? Can you provide an example code snippet that utilizes natural language processing techniques to analyze the content of an email and determine its likelihood of being spam? Additionally, how can we incorporate machine learning models to improve the accuracy of our detection algorithm?
Here's a code snippet in Go that uses natural language processing techniques to detect spam emails:
```
package main
import (
    "fmt"
    "regexp"
    "strings"
)
func main() {
    email := "Get rich quick! Buy now and save!"
    // Convert email to lowercase and remove punctuation
    cleanedEmail := strings.ToLower(email)
    cleanedEmail = regexp.MustCompile(`[^a-zA-Z0-9 ]`).ReplaceAllString(cleanedEmail, "")
    // Check for spam keywords
    keywords := []string{"buy", "rich", "save"}
    spamCount := 0
    for _, keyword := range keywords {
        if strings.Contains(cleanedEmail, keyword) {
            spamCount++
        }
    }
    // Determine likelihood of spam
    spamThreshold := 0.5
    spamLikelihood := float64(spamCount) / float64(len(keywords))
    if spamLikelihood > spamThreshold {
        fmt.Println("This email is likely spam")
    } else {
        fmt.Println("This email is not likely spam")
    }
}
```
