One possible approach is to use the Apache POI library to read the Excel table and store the original words and their corresponding synonyms in a HashMap. Then, you can use the String.replaceAll() method to replace every instance of each original word with its corresponding synonym.
Here's an example code snippet that demonstrates this approach:
```
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;
import org.apache.poi.ss.usermodel.Cell;
import org.apache.poi.ss.usermodel.Row;
import org.apache.poi.ss.usermodel.Sheet;
import org.apache.poi.ss.usermodel.Workbook;
import org.apache.poi.xssf.usermodel.XSSFWorkbook;
public class SynonymReplacer {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        // Load the Excel table
        FileInputStream file = new FileInputStream("synonyms.xlsx");
        Workbook workbook = new XSSFWorkbook(file);
        Sheet sheet = workbook.getSheetAt(0);
        // Store the original words and their synonyms in a HashMap
        Map<String, String> synonyms = new HashMap<>();
        for (Row row : sheet) {
            Cell originalWordCell = row.getCell(0);
            Cell synonymCell = row.getCell(1);
            String originalWord = originalWordCell.getStringCellValue().trim();
            String synonym = synonymCell.getStringCellValue().trim();
            synonyms.put(originalWord, synonym);
        }
        // Replace every instance of each original word with its corresponding synonym
        String text = "The police closed the streets accordingly.";
        for (String originalWord : synonyms.keySet()) {
            String synonym = synonyms.get(originalWord);
            text = text.replaceAll("\\b" + originalWord + "\\b", synonym);
        }
        // Print the modified text
        System.out.println(text);
        // Close the workbook and file input stream
        workbook.close();
        file.close();
    }
}
```
In this example, the Excel table is assumed to have two columns - the first column contains the original words, and the second column contains their corresponding synonyms. The code reads the table and stores the original words and their synonyms in a HashMap called "synonyms".
Then, the code uses the String.replaceAll() method to replace every instance of each original word with its corresponding synonym. The "\\b" pattern is used to ensure that only whole words are matched, and not partial matches within other words.
Finally, the modified text is printed to the console.
Note that the code assumes that the Excel table is in the XLSX format and is located in the same directory as the Java file. You may need to modify the file path and format if your Excel table is stored in a different location or format.

